# Cloudflare Pages routing rules for the platform project.
#
# The platform build emits two HTML entries (apps/platform/vite.config.js):
#   index.html    -> marketing SPA   (root, theapp.com in prod)
#   account.html  -> account SPA     (app.theapp.com in prod)
#
# In split-host production these are served from different origins so no
# rewrites are needed. On Cloudflare Pages both files live under one
# origin, so any navigation that lands inside the account SPA (e.g.
# /account/login, /account/reset-password, deep links from password
# recovery emails) must be rewritten to /account.html for the SPA shell
# to load. The account router reads VITE_ACCOUNT_BASENAME=/account and
# handles the rest client-side.
#
# Marketing SSG pages (/, /pricing, /blog/*, etc.) are pre-rendered to
# their own index.html files by vite-react-ssg and are served directly
# without rewrites, so a marketing catch-all would mask 404s and is
# intentionally omitted.
#
# The bare /account URL is intentionally NOT listed here. Cloudflare
# Pages serves dist/account.html for /account automatically AND
# auto-strips .html extensions, so a `/account -> /account.html`
# rewrite triggers an extension-strip back to /account and loops
# (ERR_TOO_MANY_REDIRECTS). The /account/* rule below covers every
# nested SPA route (/account/login, /account/reset-password, etc.).

/account/*          /account.html   200
